## Scope
Skills are on-demand expertise. `name` must match the folder that contains `SKILL.md`.

## Three kinds
- **Tech** (`<topic>-v<major>/`, e.g. `fastify-v5`): agent-invocable. Required sections: Scope, Assumptions, Principles, Constraints, Interactions
- **Patterns** (unversioned, e.g. `composition-patterns`, `frontend-design`): agent-invocable craft and guidelines
- **Workflow** (`.agents/skills/workflow/<name>/`): slash-only. Set `disable-model-invocation: true`. One-line `description`. Not versioned. Parent catalog: `.agents/skills/workflow/SKILL.md` (lists `/plan`, `/review`; does not dispatch `/workflow plan`)

## Principles
- One primary topic per skill; independent versions = separate skills
- `name` lowercase/digits/hyphens, max 64, equals folder name
- Prefer `paths` over legacy `globs` when file-scoped
- Declarative: state what is true. Patterns over long examples
- Progressive disclosure: keep `SKILL.md` short; depth in `references/` or `PATTERNS.md`
- No repo-specific paths in tech skills. Rules override skills
- Workflow descriptions stay one line (discovery tokens are always-on)

## Hierarchy
Rules (constraints) > skills (patterns) > model

Update procedure and inventory: `apps/docu/content/docs/development/cursor-skills.mdx`. Canonical catalog: `blockmatic/basilic-skills` (installed by `pnpm setup:skills`; lock pins this catalog only).

Workflow authoring: read `.agents/skills/workflow/references/authoring.md`. Shared references stay inside the installable `workflow` tree. Use explicit inputs, task-specific steps, observable verification, and a handoff; keep simple playbooks short.
